{
  "_comment_": "OPT-IN Codex hook gates in CANONICAL form (Claude-Code-compatible hooks.json: PascalCase events, command is a path string, matcher is a tool name; verified against real codex 0.138.0 plugin hooks ~/.codex/.tmp/plugins/*/hooks.json). ⚠ THE PATHS .codex/hooks/check-loc.sh AND .codex/hooks/checkpoint-precompact.sh ARE PLACEHOLDERS: these scripts are NOT in the package. Before enabling, CREATE them (adapt from .claude/hooks/ to the Codex payload and put them in .codex/hooks/), otherwise the hook is a no-op / path error. KL-7 (live codex exec, 6 sessions): from user/repo config in HEADLESS `codex exec` hooks do NOT fire even with --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust and a correct schema — working 0.138.0 hooks = a plugin manifest + interactive TUI trust. Conclusion: on Codex a regimen hook gate DEGRADES TO ACCOUNTABILITY (on the record); for HARD enforcement prefer CI/pre-commit, not runtime hooks. Details: docs/evidence/g2-findings.md → KL-7, core/portability.md → the guarantee matrix.",
  "hooks": {
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "shell",
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": ".codex/hooks/check-loc.sh" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": ".codex/hooks/checkpoint-precompact.sh" }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
